<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds were higher but off intraday highs in late trade, pulled back by renewed weakness in U.S. Treasuries, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We were doing pretty well on the back of currency gains, but we came off later. The Bund hasn't been able to beat strong resistance at 97.00 and that hasn't helped either,&quot; said a bond trader at a Madrid brokerage. He said dealers are wary ahead of August inflation data and the Bank of Spain's repo auction, both due Friday. Most anticipate a CPI rise of 3.9 percent from 3.7 percent in July.   &quot;But then U.S. inflation later (on Friday)</p>
<p>may limit the market's reaction,&quot; the dealer said.</p>
</text>
